[
  {
    "question": "What is a system of linear equations ? When the system is consistent ? Find the condition on g, h, k that makes the system consistent.  x1 - 4x2 + 7x3 = g  3x2 - 5x3 = h   -2x1 + 5x2 - 9x3 = k",
    "answer": "<p>A system of linear equations is a collection of one or more linear equations involving one or more variables. Each equation in the system is a linear combination of the variables, and the goal is to find values for the variables that satisfy all the equations simultaneously. In general, a system of linear equations can be represented as follows:</p>\n<p>a₁x₁ + a₂x₂ + a₃x₃ + … + aₙxₙ = b₁<br />\na₁’x₁ + a₂’x₂ + a₃’x₃ + … + aₙ’xₙ = b₂<br />\na₁”x₁ + a₂”x₂ + a₃”x₃ + … + aₙ”xₙ = b₃<br />\n…<br />\na₁ᵤx₁ + a₂ᵤx₂ + a₃ᵤx₃ + … + aₙᵤxₙ = bᵤ</p>\n<p>Where:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>x₁, x₂, x₃, …, xₙ are the variables.</li>\n<li>a₁, a₂, a₃, …, aₙ are the coefficients of the variables in the first equation.</li>\n<li>b₁ is the constant on the right side of the first equation.</li>\n<li>Similarly, a₁’, a₂’, a₃’, …, aₙ’, b₂, a₁”, a₂”, a₃”, …, aₙ”, b₃, and so on represent the coefficients and constants in the subsequent equations.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A system of linear equations is consistent when it has at least one solution, which means there is a set of values for the variables that satisfies all the equations in the system. In other words, a system of equations is consistent if there is at least one combination of values for the variables that makes all the equations true simultaneously.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "$$ Let A =\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 5 \\\\ \\end{bmatrix} ,u= \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2\\\\ 3\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}, b= \\begin{bmatrix} -2\\\\ -2\\\\ \\end{bmatrix},$$  and define a transformation T : R3 → R² by T(x) = Ax then  a. find T(u).  b. Find x ∈ R3 whose image under T is b.  c. Is x unique ?",
