  {
    "question": "Find the least square solution of Ax=b where  $$ A=\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -3 & -3\\\\ 1 & 5 & 1\\\\ 1 & 7 & 2\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}, b= \\begin{bmatrix} 5\\\\ -3\\\\ 5\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$  and compute the associated least square error.",
    "answer": "<p>given,</p>\n<p>$$A =\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; -3 &amp; -3\\\\<br />\n1 &amp; 5 &amp; 1\\\\<br />\n1 &amp; 7 &amp; 2\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix} and  b = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n5\\\\<br />\n-3\\\\<br />\n-5\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>now,</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">x = (A<sup>T</sup> A)<sup>-1</sup> (A<sup>T</sup> b) _______(1)</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A<sup>T </sup>= \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 1 &amp; 1\\\\<br />\n-3 &amp; 5 &amp; 7\\\\<br />\n-3 &amp; 1 &amp; 2\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A<sup>T</sup>A = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 1 &amp; 1\\\\<br />\n-3 &amp; 5 &amp; 7\\\\<br />\n-3 &amp; 1 &amp; 2\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; -3 &amp; -3\\\\<br />\n1 &amp; 5 &amp; 1\\\\<br />\n1 &amp; 7 &amp; 2\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A<sup>T</sup>A = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n3 &amp; 9 &amp; 0\\\\<br />\n9 &amp; 83 &amp; 28\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 28 &amp; 14\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">here,</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A<sup>T</sup>b = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 1 &amp; 1\\\\<br />\n-3 &amp; 5 &amp; 7\\\\<br />\n-3 &amp; 1 &amp; 2\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n5\\\\<br />\n-3\\\\<br />\n-5\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A<sup>T</sup>b =\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n-3\\\\<br />\n-65\\\\<br />\n-28\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}</p>\n<p>Since we have definition of least square; the set of least square solutions of Ax = b coincides with the non-empty set of solutions of A<sup>T</sup>Ax = A<sup>T</sup>b</p>\n<p>therefore,</p>\n<p><span id=\"MJXc-Node-860\" class=\"mjx-texatom\"><span id=\"MJXc-Node-861\" class=\"mjx-mrow\"><span id=\"MJXc-Node-862\" class=\"mjx-munderover\"><span class=\"mjx-stack\"><span class=\"mjx-op\"><span id=\"MJXc-Node-863\" class=\"mjx-mi\"><span class=\"mjx-char MJXc-TeX-math-I\">x </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span id=\"MJXc-Node-865\" class=\"mjx-mo MJXc-space3\"><span class=\"mjx-char MJXc-TeX-main-R\">= (A<sup>T</sup> A)<sup>-1</sup> (A<sup>T</sup> b)</span></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">|A<sup>T</sup> A |= |\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n3 &amp; 9 &amp; 0\\\\<br />\n9 &amp; 83 &amp; 28\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 28 &amp; 14\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}| = 0</p>\n<p>Since, |A<sup>T</sup> A |<span id=\"MJXc-Node-873\" class=\"mjx-msubsup\"><span class=\"mjx-base\"><span id=\"MJXc-Node-874\" class=\"mjx-mo\"><span class=\"mjx-char MJXc-TeX-main-R\"> = 0 </span></span></span></span><span id=\"MJXc-Node-873\" class=\"mjx-msubsup\"><span class=\"mjx-base\"><span id=\"MJXc-Node-874\" class=\"mjx-mo\"><span class=\"mjx-char MJXc-TeX-main-R\">so, inverse doesn&#8217;t exists. </span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span id=\"MJXc-Node-873\" class=\"mjx-msubsup\"><span class=\"mjx-base\"><span id=\"MJXc-Node-874\" class=\"mjx-mo\"><span class=\"mjx-char MJXc-TeX-main-R\">Hence, there is no solution.</span></span></span></span></p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Are vectors $$v_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1//4//0// \\end{bmatrix}, v_2=\\begin{bmatrix}10//2//1// \\end{bmatrix} and v_3=\\begin{bmatrix}-5//0//6// \\end{bmatrix}$$ linearly independent? Justify.",
    "answer": "<p>given,</p>\n<p>$$v_1=\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1\\\\<br />\n4\\\\<br />\n0\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix},<br />\nv_2=\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n10\\\\<br />\n2\\\\<br />\n1\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix} and<br />\nv_3=<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n-5\\\\<br />\n0\\\\<br />\n6\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>augmented matrix will be as,</p>\n<p>$$\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 10 &amp; -5\\\\<br />\n4 &amp; 2 &amp;0\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 1 &amp; 6\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>Applying R<sub>2</sub> → R<sub>2 </sub>&#8211; 4R<sub>1</sub></p>\n<p>$$∼ \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 10 &amp; -5\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; -38 &amp; 20\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 1 &amp; 6\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>Applying R<sub>2</sub> → R<sub>2</sub>/ (-38)</p>\n<p>$$∼ \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 10 &amp; -5\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; -38 &amp; \\frac{{-20}}{{38}}\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 1 &amp; 6\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>Applying R<sub>1</sub> → R<sub>1 </sub>&#8211; 10R<sub>2</sub> , R<sub>3</sub> → R<sub>3 </sub>&#8211; R<sub>2</sub></p>\n<p>$$∼ \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 0 &amp; \\frac{{5}}{{19}}\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 1 &amp; \\frac{{-20}}{{38}}\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\frac{{124}}{{19}}\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>Applying R<sub>3</sub> → R<sub>3</sub>/ (19/124)</p>\n<p>$$∼ \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 0 &amp; \\frac{{5}}{{19}}\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 1 &amp; \\frac{{-20}}{{38}}\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>Applying R<sub>1</sub> → R<sub>1 </sub>&#8211; (5/19)R<sub>3</sub> , R<sub>2</sub> → R<sub>2 </sub>+ (20/38)R<sub>3</sub></p>\n<p>$$∼ \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0\\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1\\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>As the solution is non trival so, we can say that the soln is linearly independent.</p>\n"
  },
