    "question": " Let u = (1, -2, 2, 0). Find a unit vector of  v  in the same direction of u.",
    "answer": "<p>To find the unit vector in the same direction as a vector, we divide it by its magnitude.</p>\n<p>The magnitude of \\( \\vec{v} \\) is<br />\n$$ \\sqrt{1^2 + (-2)^2 + 2^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{9} = 3 $$</p>\n<p>We will divide vector \\( \\vec{u} \\) by the magnitude of vector \\( \\vec{v} \\). So,</p>\n<p>$$ \\left( \\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{-2}{3}, \\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{0}{3} \\right) $$</p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Find LU Factorization. Given the matrix: $$ \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} $$",
    "answer": "<p>$$\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 \\\\<br />\n4 &amp; 5 &amp; 10 \\\\<br />\n4 &amp; 8 &amp; 2<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Step 1: Perform row operations to simplify the matrix. R<sub>2</sub> → R<sub>2</sub> &#8211; 2R<sub>1</sub>,  R<sub>3</sub> → R<sub>3</sub> &#8211; 2R<sub>1</sub><br />\n$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; -1 &amp; 2 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 2 &amp; -6<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Step 1: Perform row operations to simplify the matrix. R<sub>3</sub> → R<sub>3</sub> + 2R<sub>2</sub></p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; -1 &amp; 2 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; -2<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Pivot element of first column is 2</p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 \\\\<br />\n4 \\\\<br />\n4 \\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix} / 2 = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 \\\\<br />\n2 \\\\<br />\n2 \\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Pivot element of second column is -1</p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n-1 \\\\<br />\n2 \\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix} / -1 = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 \\\\<br />\n-2 \\\\<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Pivot element of second column is -1</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[-2] / -2 = [1]</p>\n<p>LU Factorization:<br />\n$$<br />\nL = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\\\<br />\n2 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 \\\\<br />\n2 &amp; -2 &amp; 1<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad<br />\nU = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; -1 &amp; 2 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; -2<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Define group. Show that (Ζ , .) doesn't form a group.",
    "answer": "<p>A group is a fundamental algebraic structure in abstract algebra that consists of a set together with an operation that combines elements from the set and satisfies four key properties:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Closure</strong>: For any two elements, a and b, in the group, their combination under the group operation must also be in the group. In other words, a . b is an element of the group.</li>\n<li><strong>Associativity</strong>: The group operation is associative, which means that for any three elements a, b, and c in the group, the following equality holds: (a . b) . c = a . (b . c).</li>\n<li><strong>Identity Element</strong>: There exists an identity element, denoted as “e” or “1,” such that for any element “a” in the group, the following equation is true: a . e = e . a = a.</li>\n<li><strong>Inverse Element</strong>: For each element “a” in the group, there exists an inverse element “b” such that a . b = b . a = e, where “e” is the identity element.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Now,</p>\n<p>The set of integers, denoted as Z, is checked if it form a group with respect to the multiplication operation (.) or not:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Closure</strong>: For any two integers “a” and “b,” their product “a . b” is also an integer. Therefore, closure is satisfied.</li>\n<li><strong>Associativity</strong>: Multiplication of integers is associative, meaning that for any integers “a,” “b,” and “c,” we have<br />\n(a . b) . c = a . (b . c)<br />\nThis property holds.</li>\n<li><strong>Identity Element</strong>: The identity element for multiplication in the set of integers is “0”. For any integer “a,” we have<br />\na . 1 = 1 . a = a<br />\nTherefore, the identity element is present.</li>\n<li><strong>Inverse Element</strong>: For every integer “a,” its inverse with respect to multiplication is “1/a”.<br />\nHere, the inverse 1/a isn&#8217;t an integer. So, group is not formed.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Since, the set of integers doesn&#8217;t hold all four properties of a group with respect to multiplication, it is not a group under multiplication.</p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Is $$\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\2\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$ an eigen vector of  $$\\begin{bmatrix}5&-3\\\\-4&9\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$ ? If so, find eigenvalue.",
    "answer": "<p>$$A =\\begin{bmatrix} 5 &amp; -3\\\\ -4 &amp;9\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}, X =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\ 2\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>$$AX = \\begin{bmatrix} 5 &amp; -3\\\\ -4 &amp;9\\\\ \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} 3\\\\ 2\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>$$AX = \\begin{bmatrix} 9\\\\ 6\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>$$AX = 3 \\begin{bmatrix} 3\\\\ 2\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$</p>\n<p>Hence, $$\\begin{bmatrix} 3\\\\ 2\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$ is eigen vector of $$\\begin{bmatrix} 5 &amp; -3\\\\ -4 &amp;9\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}$$.</p>\n<p>now,</p>\n<p>for eigen value charactristics equation is</p>\n<p>$$|A &#8211; λI| = 0$$</p>\n<p>$$|\\begin{bmatrix} 5 &amp; -3\\\\ -4 &amp;9\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}-λ\\begin{bmatrix} 1 &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp;1\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}| = 0$$</p>\n<p>$$|\\begin{bmatrix} 5 &amp; -3\\\\ -4 &amp;9\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix} λ &amp; 0\\\\ 0 &amp;λ\\\\ \\end{bmatrix}| = 0$$</p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-43100 aligncenter\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Vcnn6Ccf/793cbbe615d1.jpg\" alt=\"- Hamro CSIT\" width=\"187\" height=\"194\"></p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Compute Det of A where $$\\[ A = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -8 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 5 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\end{bmatrix} \\]$$",
    "answer": "<p>Given the matrix:<br />\n$$<br />\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; -8 &amp; 6 &amp; 8 \\\\<br />\n3 &amp; -9 &amp; 5 &amp; 10 \\\\<br />\n-3 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; -2 \\\\<br />\n1 &amp; -4 &amp; 0 &amp; 6<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Perform row operations to simplify the matrix. R<sub>4</sub> → R<sub>4</sub> &#8211; 1/3R<sub>2 </sub>, R<sub>3</sub> → R<sub>3</sub> + R<sub>2</sub></p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; -8 &amp; 6 &amp; 8 \\\\<br />\n3 &amp; -9 &amp; 5 &amp; 10 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; -9 &amp; 6 &amp; 8 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; -1 &amp; -5/3 &amp; 8/3<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Perform row operations to simplify the matrix. R<sub>2</sub> → R<sub>2</sub> &#8211; 3/2R<sub>1</sub>,  R<sub>4</sub> → R<sub>4</sub> + 1/3R<sub>2 </sub>, R<sub>3</sub> → R<sub>3</sub> + 3R<sub>2</sub><br />\n$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; -8 &amp; 6 &amp; 8 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 3 &amp; -4 &amp; -2 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; -6 &amp; 2 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; -3 &amp; 2<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Continue simplifying to upper triangular form to compute the determinant:<br />\n$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n2 &amp; -8 &amp; 6 &amp; 8 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 3 &amp; -4 &amp; -2 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; -6 &amp; 2 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 3/2<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>The determinant is calculated by multiplying the diagonal elements.<br />\n$$<br />\n\\text{det}(A) = 2 \\times 3 \\times (-6) \\times \\frac{3}{2} = -54<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Show that H = {(a−3b, b−a, a, b) : a, b ∈ R} is a subspace of  R4.",
    "answer": "<p>To show that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">H</span></span> is a subspace of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">R<sup>4</sup></span></span>, we need to verify the following conditions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The zero vector <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">0 ∈ H</span></span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">H</span></span> is closed under vector addition.</li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">H</span></span> is closed under scalar multiplication.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">v = (a−3b, b−a, a, b)</span></span></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Zero Vector</strong>:<br />\nSet <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a = 0 </span></span>and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">b = 0</span></span>. Then:<br />\n<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">v </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0 </span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\">0 </span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)<br />\nSo, the zero vector is in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">H</span></span>, i.e., <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">0 ∈ H</span></span>.</span></span></li>\n<li><strong>Closed under Addition</strong>:<br />\nLet <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">v1=(a<sub>1 </sub>− 3b<sub>1</sub>, b<sub>1 </sub>− a<sub>1</sub>, a<sub>1</sub>, b<sub>1</sub>)</span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">v2 = (a<sub>2 </sub>− 3b<sub>2</sub>, b<sub>2 </sub>− a<sub>2</sub>, a<sub>2</sub>, b<sub>2</sub>) </span></span>be two vectors in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">H</span></span>. The sum is:<br />\n<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">v</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">v</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">((</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2 </span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)<br />\n</span></span></span>Simplifying:<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">= ((a<sub>1 </sub>+ a<sub>2</sub>) − 3(b<sub>1 </sub>+ b<sub>2</sub>), (b<sub>1 </sub>+ b<sub>2</sub>) − (a<sub>1 </sub>+ a<sub>2</sub>), a<sub>1 </sub>+ a<sub>2</sub>, b<sub>1 </sub>+ b<sub>2</sub>)<br />\nThis is of the same form as (a − 3b, b − a, a, b), so v<sub>1</sub> + v<sub>2</sub> ∈ H.</span></span></span></span></span></li>\n<li><strong>Closed under Scalar Multiplication</strong>:<br />\nLet <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c ∈ R </span></span>and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">v = (a − 3b, b − a, a, b)</span></span>. Then:<br />\n<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">v </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a </span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b </span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a </span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b </span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mpunct\">, </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">)<br />\n</span></span></span>Simplifying:<br />\n= (ca − 3cb, cb − ca, ca, cb)<br />\nThis is also of the form <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">(a − 3b, b − a, a, b)</span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">cv ∈ H.</span></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Thus, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">H</span></span> is a subspace of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">R<sup>4</sup></span></span>.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Find the basis and dimension of Nul A where A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\end{bmatrix}.",
    "answer": "<p>To find the basis of the null space <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">Nul A</span></span>, we need to solve the homogeneous system <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">Ax = 0</span></span>, where :</p>\n<p>$$<br />\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 \\\\<br />\n2 &amp; 4 &amp; 7 &amp; 8<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad<br />\n\\mathbf{x} = \\begin{bmatrix}<br />\nx_1 \\\\<br />\nx_2 \\\\<br />\nx_3 \\\\<br />\nx_4<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>We write the augmented matrix for the system <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">Ax = 0 :</span></span></p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp;| 0 \\\\<br />\n2 &amp; 4 &amp; 7 &amp; 8 &amp;| 0<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>Perform row reduction:</p>\n<p>Subtract 2 times the first row from the second row:</p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix}<br />\n1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp;| 0 \\\\<br />\n0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp;| 0<br />\n\\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>The system now becomes:</p>\n<p><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><sub><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></sub></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><sub><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></sub></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0 </span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(Row 1)</span></span></span><br />\n<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><sub><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3 </span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></sub></span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0 </span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(Row 2)</span></span></span></p>\n<p>From Row 2, we have <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><sub><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></sub></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>. Substituting into Row 1:</p>\n<p><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0   </span><span class=\"mrel\">⇒   </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><sub><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></sub></span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​ </span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">− </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><sub><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Thus, the solution is:</p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix} -2x_2 &#8211; 4x_4 \\\\ x_2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ x_4 \\end{bmatrix} = x_2 \\begin{bmatrix} -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} + x_4 \\begin{bmatrix} -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>The null space basis is:</p>\n<p>$$<br />\n\\begin{bmatrix} -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix} -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}<br />\n$$</p>\n<p>The dimension of \\( \\text{Nul } A \\) is 2.</p>\n<p><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"delimsizing mult\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n"
  },
  {
    "question": "Show that every field is an integral domain.",
    "answer": "<p>To show that every field is an integral domain, let&#8217;s recall the definitions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>field</strong> is a set with two operations (addition and multiplication) where every element (except 0) has a multiplicative inverse.</li>\n<li>An <strong>integral domain</strong> is a commutative ring with no zero divisors, meaning if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">ab = 0</span></span>, then either <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a = 0</span></span> or <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">b = 0</span></span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Now, let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">F</span></span> be a field, and consider two elements <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">aa</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">b</span></span> in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">F</span></span> such that:</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">ab = 0</span></span></span></p>\n<p>We need to show that either <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a = 0 </span></span>or <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">b = 0</span></span>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a = 0</span></span>, the equation is trivially true.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a ≠ 0</span></span>, then since <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">F</span></span> is a field, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">aa</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span></span></span></span> has a multiplicative inverse <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a<sup>−1</sup></span></span> in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">F</span></span>. Multiplying both sides of the equation <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">ab = 0</span></span> by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a<sup>−1</sup></span></span>:</li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a<sup>−1</sup>(ab) = a<sup>−1</sup>⋅0</span></span></span></p>\n<p>Simplifying:</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">b = 0</span></span></span></p>\n<p>Thus, in a field, if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">ab = 0</span></span>, then either <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a = 0 </span></span>or <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">b = 0</span></span>. Therefore, a field has no zero divisors, which means every field is an integral domain.</p>\n"
  }
]